/* book Worked example 2: Q: An S-band surveillance radar works at 3 GHz with Pt = 1.5 MW, G = 33 dB, receiver bandwidth 1 MHz, noise figure 4 dB, required single-pulse (S/N)min = 13 dB and system loss 6 dB. Find Smin, then Rmax for a 2 m² aircraft. How far does it reach if 10 pulses are integrated coherently?
   1. Ratios: F = 100.4 = 2.512, (S/N)min = 101.3 = 19.95, G = 103.3 = 1995, L = 100.6 = 3.981; λ = 0.1 m.
   2. Noise floor: kT0BF = 1.38 × 10⁻²³ × 290 × 10⁶ × 2.512 = 1.005 × 10⁻¹⁴ W.
   3. Smin = 1.005 × 10⁻¹⁴ × 19.95 = 2.006 × 10⁻¹³ W, which is −127.0 dBW.
   4. Budget in dB: Pt 61.76 + 2G 66.0 + λ² −20.0 + σ 3.01 − (4π)³ 32.98 − Smin (−127.0) − L 6.0 = 198.77 dB.
   5. Rmax = 10198.77/40 = 93 176 m = 93.2 km.
   6. Coherent integration of 10 pulses lowers the needed Smin by 10, so Rmax grows by 101/4 = 1.778 to 165.7 km.
   Answer: Smin = 2.0 × 10⁻¹³ W (−127 dBW); Rmax = 93.2 km on one pulse and 165.7 km with 10 pulses integrated coherently. */
