/* book exam traps: Taking the noise floor kT0BF as the minimum detectable signal. Detection needs the floor times (S/N)min; leaving it out makes Rmax too large by (S/N)min1/4, a factor of 2.1 for 13 dB. | Forgetting that G is squared. A 3 dB gain error becomes 6 dB in the echo. | Doubling range with doubled power. It takes 16 times the power, 12 dB more. | Putting F or G in dB into a ratio formula. 10 dB means a ratio of 10, and 30 dB a ratio of 1000. | Mixing units: λ in cm or R in km in a formula written for metres. */
