/* book exam traps: Reading σ as physical area. "The target is 1 m²" means nothing without the band and the aspect. | Carrying a σ value from one band to another. A 1 m nose is in the resonance region at VHF (λ of a few metres) and in the optical region at X band, with very different σ. | Reading 0 dBsm as zero area. It is 1 m²; −20 dBsm is 0.01 m². | Using σ = 4πA²/λ² off normal incidence. A few degrees away the in-phase sum collapses. | Calling ka = 5 the optical region. The optical formula πa² is reliable only above ka ≈ 10. */
